---
/**
 * Shown only to visitors the law actually covers — the EEA, the UK and
 * Switzerland — and only until they answer once. Everyone else never sees it,
 * because Consent Mode already treats their region as granted.
 *
 * Rendered hidden and revealed by script, rather than built in JS, so the
 * markup is in the HTML for screen readers and the styles are in the sheet
 * that has already loaded. There is no layout shift either way: it is fixed
 * to the bottom of the viewport.
 */
---
<div
  class="consent"
  data-consent
  hidden
  role="dialog"
  aria-labelledby="consent-title"
  aria-describedby="consent-body"
>
  <div class="consent__inner">
    <div>
      <p class="consent__title" id="consent-title">A word about cookies</p>
      <p class="consent__body" id="consent-body">
        Analytics cookies tell me which itineraries actually get read, and
        which ones to write next. Say no and the site behaves exactly the
        same — nothing here is gated. <a href="/privacy/">What gets collected</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="consent__actions">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-consent-choice="denied">
        Reject
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--solid" data-consent-choice="granted">
        Accept
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
